    {
      "type": "derive",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "title": "Where the range comes from",
      "tags": [
        "correlation-bounds"
      ],
      "pace": 150,
      "prose": "Put the argument in order, as you would at a whiteboard. One line does not belong.",
      "question": "Order the steps that give the range of $c$.",
      "widget": {
        "kind": "order",
        "lines": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "Write the correlation matrix $R$: ones on the diagonal, and $a$, $b$, $c$ off it."
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "With $|a| < 1$ the top-left $2 \\times 2$ block is positive definite, so $R$ is valid exactly when $\\det R \\ge 0$."
          },
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "Expand: $\\det R = 1 + 2abc - a^2 - b^2 - c^2$."
          },
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "Read it as a quadratic in $c$ that must be at least 0: $-c^2 + 2ab\\,c + 1 - a^2 - b^2$."
          },
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "By the quadratic formula its roots are $ab \\pm \\sqrt{(1 - a^2)(1 - b^2)}$."
          },
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "The quadratic opens downwards, so $c$ must lie between the roots."
          },
          {
            "id": "d1",
            "text": "Each entry lies in $[-1, 1]$, so every $c$ in $[-1, 1]$ is allowed.",
            "why": "That checks the entries one at a time. A matrix can have every entry in range and still a negative eigenvalue."
          }
        ],
        "answer": [
          "s1",
          "s2",
          "s3",
          "s4",
          "s5",
          "s6"
        ],
        "distractors": [
          "d1"
        ]
      },
      "hints": [
        {
          "rung": "nudge",
          "text": "Start from the matrix, then the condition on it."
        },
        {
          "rung": "point",
          "text": "The condition is a quadratic in $c$."
        },
        {
          "rung": "step",
          "text": "A downward quadratic is at least 0 between its roots."
        }
      ],
      "feedback": {
        "correct": "Matrix, condition, quadratic, roots.",
        "generic": "Not quite right. Write the matrix, state the condition, then solve for $c$.",
        "byKey": {
          "d1": "You checked the entries one at a time. The matrix as a whole must have no negative eigenvalue.",
          "left-out": "You left out a line that belongs. Only one line is wrong."
        }
      },
      "explain": {
        "text": "The determinant is a downward quadratic in $c$. It is at least 0 between its two roots, $ab \\pm \\sqrt{(1 - a^2)(1 - b^2)}$. Outside them some portfolio would have negative variance."
      }
    },
